[{"role": "system", "content": "Propose the actions people can attempt so the listed behaviors can happen. An action is something a person chooses to try (hold a meeting, reopen an issue, attach a condition to support, vote, deploy); things that happen on their own each tick are processes and are not actions. Do not repeat an existing action or propose another that does what one already does. Fields name the entities or values the attempt needs (entity_ref for an entity); the person attempting it is implied, so never add an actor field. Name in for_behaviors the request_ids each action serves. Preserve independent technical condition, report lineage, delivery, personal stance, recorded assent and public hold. Residents choose their responses. No rule may force a stance or assent from evidence, require conflict or agreement, or turn elapsed time into successful repair. The compiled independent procedure owns technical intervention, authorized validation, hold, public positions and assent; do not duplicate or write those components. Additional actions express choices or practical tasks explicitly requested by the scenario. Waiting is permitted."}, {"role": "user", "content": "{
