[{"role": "system", "content": "You are proposing causal mechanics for a governed world model. Return exactly one JSON object and no prose or markdown. You are not writing code. mechanics must hold one mechanic for each of these moves: request-evidence, investigate-claim, author-report; an empty mechanics list is always rejected. The response must satisfy response_contract. Every effect must be justified by represented state and the action description. Prefer conservative refusal checks over assumptions. Do not add reads/writes fields; the local compiler derives authority. Whenever you name a state path, copy it EXACTLY from allowed_state_paths. Where one change physically sets off another at once (a fall, a break, a spill, a noise heard nearby), write that consequence as a process with timing immediately."}, {"role": "user", "content": "{
  "actions": [
    {
      "description": "Request a specific evidence item; this does not itself deliver the evidence or change the pump's technical condition.",
      "fields": [
        {
          "name": "evidence",
          "type": "entity_ref"
        }
      ],
      "kind": "request-evidence"
    },
    {
